# aurora.local / packages/notes/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/notes/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/notes/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# ghcr.io/silverbulletmd/silverbullet — pinned to 2.9.0 (not 2.10.0).
#
# 2.10.0 is the newer release (published 2026-07-28) and was the pin
# originally recorded here on 2026-08-15. It's since been withdrawn:
# 2.10 is the "MultiSpace" rearchitecture, and in single-space mode
# (SB_USER set) the client boot fetches /index.json before a session
# is established, gets 302'd to /.auth (HTML), tries to parse the
# HTML as JSON, and crashes with:
#
#   Could not process config and no cached copy, please connect
#   to the Internet
#
# See upstream issues #1724 and #1752, and PR #1750 which fixes
# adjacent 5xx boot-lockouts but not the auth-redirect variant.
# The community thread for 2.10 has multiple reports of the same
# rollback (https://community.silverbullet.md/t/4282). Aurora
# leaves SB_USER absent by default (Authelia gates the vhost) so
# 2.10 boots fine in that shape too — but keeping the pin on the
# last known-good pre-MultiSpace release means a box that opts
# into standalone auth (Option B in packages/notes/README.md)
# doesn't fall into the same trap.
#
# Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — confirmed
# via `docker buildx imagetools inspect`. Checked 2026-08-26.
IMAGE_SILVERBULLET=ghcr.io/silverbulletmd/silverbullet:2.9.0@sha256:82e76a800920370d83e2f50c6946d3c420954b0bd417dbb96f7911513fa05620
